From b96237509679aa75c979d2ebd0c4924a8f8d5964 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Keith Busch <kbusch@kernel.org>
Date: Tue, 19 May 2026 18:03:44 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 20/60] nvme-pci: fix dma_vecs leak on p2p memory

[ Upstream commit 85686c72966c5ee637893f124ddb31a1cace7bee ]

We don't unmap P2P memory, so we don't need to track it. The dma_vec
allocation was getting leaked on the completion.

Fixes: b8b7570a7ec87 ("nvme-pci: fix dma unmapping when using PRPs and not using the IOVA mapping")
Reviewed-by: Christoph Hellwig <hch@lst.de>
Signed-off-by: Keith Busch <kbusch@kernel.org>
Signed-off-by: Sasha Levin <sashal@kernel.org>
(cherry picked from commit 24ea0de233d9ebb5ebd6f6018eaf2084af25e3dd)

[ Adapted for this branch: upstream checks (iod->flags & IOD_DATA_P2P),
  but that flag was introduced later by commit 37f0c7a8df7ad
  ("block-dma: properly take MMIO path"), which is not present on this
  branch. This branch already tracks the identical condition -- a
  request mapped via PCI_P2PDMA_MAP_BUS_ADDR, for which no DMA unmap is
  ever required -- through req->cmd_flags & REQ_P2PDMA, which is the
  exact same check already used by blk_dma_unmap() in
  include/linux/blk-mq-dma.h for this purpose. Use that existing
  equivalent instead of pulling in the unrelated MMIO-path refactor. ]
Signed-off-by: CVE Backport Agent
---
 drivers/nvme/host/pci.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

Index: b/drivers/nvme/host/pci.c
===================================================================
--- a/drivers/nvme/host/pci.c
+++ b/drivers/nvme/host/pci.c
@@ -827,7 +827,8 @@ static bool nvme_pci_prp_save_mapping(st
 {
 	struct nvme_iod *iod = blk_mq_rq_to_pdu(req);
 
-	if (dma_use_iova(&iod->dma_state) || !dma_need_unmap(dma_dev))
+	if (dma_use_iova(&iod->dma_state) || !dma_need_unmap(dma_dev) ||
+            (iod->flags & IOD_DATA_P2P))
 		return true;
 
 	if (!iod->nr_dma_vecs) {
